IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc1-prelim`
IMPORT `ssc1-class1`

-- Tests for ssc1-class1.l4 (ss 5 to 9B). Every expected value is written from the text beside the assertion.
-- The limits below are STAND-IN figures for the tests only (the Act leaves the real ones to regulations, s 5(1)):
-- lower earnings limit 100, primary threshold 200, upper earnings limit 1000, secondary threshold 150.

§ `Tests for ss 5 to 9B`

`ssc1 fixture person` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1990
    `sex` IS Man
    `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2056

`ssc1 fixture contract of service` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `ssc1 fixture person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 4 2020
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS TRUE
    `held in an office` IS FALSE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

`ssc1 fixture own business` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `ssc1 fixture person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `an individual`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 4 2020
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS FALSE
    `held in an office` IS FALSE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

`ssc1 fixture office` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `ssc1 fixture person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `a government department, public authority or other body of persons`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 4 2020
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS FALSE
    `held in an office` IS TRUE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

`ssc1 fixture year 2030` MEANS `Tax year` OF 2030
`ssc1 fixture year 2031` MEANS `Tax year` OF 2031
`ssc1 fixture limits 2030` MEANS `Earnings limits` OF `ssc1 fixture year 2030`, 100, 200, 1000, 150
`ssc1 fixture limits 2031` MEANS `Earnings limits` OF `ssc1 fixture year 2031`, 110, 210, 1010, 160
`ssc1 fixture week 10 of 2030` MEANS `Tax week` OF `ssc1 fixture year 2030`, 10

-- `Earnings paid` OF amount, tax week
`ssc1 fixture paid` amount MEANS `Earnings paid` OF amount, `ssc1 fixture week 10 of 2030`

§§ `s 5`

-- s 5(1): the list holds the limits for 2030 and 2031: 2031 finds the 2031 limits; 2032 finds none (outside the text).
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the limits and thresholds for the tax year` (LIST `ssc1 fixture limits 2030`, `ssc1 fixture limits 2031`) `ssc1 fixture year 2031` EQUALS JUST `ssc1 fixture limits 2031`
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the limits and thresholds for the tax year` (LIST `ssc1 fixture limits 2030`, `ssc1 fixture limits 2031`) `ssc1 fixture year 2030` EQUALS JUST `ssc1 fixture limits 2030`
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the limits and thresholds for the tax year` (LIST `ssc1 fixture limits 2030`, `ssc1 fixture limits 2031`) (`Tax year` OF 2032) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 5(1)(a), (b): the four figures come from the record
#ASSERT `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 5(1)(a) the primary threshold in force at the time in pounds` `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 5(1)(a) the upper earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `s 5(1)(b) the secondary threshold in force at the time in pounds` `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` EQUALS 150
-- s 5(4): weekly earners get the weekly limits; others the prescribed equivalents, if prescribed
#ASSERT `s 5(4) the limits and thresholds that apply to the earner` `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST `ssc1 fixture limits 2031`) FALSE EQUALS JUST `ssc1 fixture limits 2030`
#ASSERT `s 5(4) the limits and thresholds that apply to the earner` `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST `ssc1 fixture limits 2031`) TRUE EQUALS JUST `ssc1 fixture limits 2031`
#ASSERT `s 5(4) the limits and thresholds that apply to the earner` `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 5(5): an equivalent may exceed the arithmetical equivalent by not more than 1.00
#ASSERT `s 5(5) the regulations may prescribe the amount as an equivalent of the limit or threshold` 101 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(5) the regulations may prescribe the amount as an equivalent of the limit or threshold` 100.99 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(5) the regulations may prescribe the amount as an equivalent of the limit or threshold` 101.01 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(5) the regulations may prescribe the amount as an equivalent of the limit or threshold` 100 100 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 6`

-- s 6(1)(a): primary payable if the amount EXCEEDS the primary threshold (200). 200.01 exceeds; 200 does not.
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(a) a primary Class 1 contribution is payable in accordance with sections 6 and 8` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 200.01) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(a) a primary Class 1 contribution is payable in accordance with sections 6 and 8` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 200) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(a) a primary Class 1 contribution is payable in accordance with sections 6 and 8` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 199) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- outside the opening words: an earner not over 16 (s 173(a) says no), not an employed earner's employment, limits of another year, K2 unanswered: not covered
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(a) a primary Class 1 contribution is payable in accordance with sections 6 and 8` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 500) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST FALSE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(a) a primary Class 1 contribution is payable in accordance with sections 6 and 8` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 500) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture own business` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(a) a primary Class 1 contribution is payable in accordance with sections 6 and 8` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 500) `ssc1 fixture limits 2031` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(a) a primary Class 1 contribution is payable in accordance with sections 6 and 8` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 500) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` NOTHING `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an office with earnings counts as employed earner's employment
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(a) a primary Class 1 contribution is payable in accordance with sections 6 and 8` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 500) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture office` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 6(1)(b): secondary payable if the amount EXCEEDS the secondary threshold (150)
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) a secondary Class 1 contribution is payable in accordance with sections 6 and 9` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 150.01) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) a secondary Class 1 contribution is payable in accordance with sections 6 and 9` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 150) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) a secondary Class 1 contribution is payable in accordance with sections 6 and 9` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 150.01) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST FALSE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the earner's own primary threshold (200) is above the secondary (150): 180 pays secondary but not primary
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(a) a primary Class 1 contribution is payable in accordance with sections 6 and 8` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 180) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) a secondary Class 1 contribution is payable in accordance with sections 6 and 9` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 180) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 6(2)
#ASSERT `s 6(2) a primary or secondary Class 1 contribution is payable in respect of the earnings` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(2) a primary or secondary Class 1 contribution is payable in respect of the earnings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6(3): after pensionable age no primary contribution, unless prescribed otherwise
#ASSERT `s 6(3) a primary Class 1 contribution is payable in respect of the earnings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(3) a primary Class 1 contribution is payable in respect of the earnings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(3) a primary Class 1 contribution is payable in respect of the earnings` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6(4)
#ASSERT `s 6(4) who is liable to pay the Class 1 contribution` `Class 1 primary` FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 6(4)(a) the earner`
#ASSERT `s 6(4) who is liable to pay the Class 1 contribution` `Class 1 secondary` FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 6(4)(b) the secondary contributor`
#ASSERT `s 6(4) who is liable to pay the Class 1 contribution` `Class 1 primary` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(4) who is liable to pay the Class 1 contribution` `Class 2` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6(5): other employments are ignored unless the Act provides otherwise
#ASSERT `s 6(5) the earnings counted for this employment` 300 500 FALSE EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `s 6(5) the earnings counted for this employment` 300 500 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the bar combiner: a bar that says no wins; a bar that does not engage (NOTHING) leaves the grant standing
#ASSERT `s 6 the answer once a bar is taken into account` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6 the answer once a bar is taken into account` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6 the answer once a bar is taken into account` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6 the answer once a bar is taken into account` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 6 whole: primary payable on 500 when no bar applies (residence met, no Class 1B, not past pensionable age)
#ASSERT `s 6 a primary Class 1 contribution is payable, having regard to sections 1(6)(a), 6(2) and 6(3)` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 500) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- residence conditions not met: barred by s 1(6)(a)
#ASSERT `s 6 a primary Class 1 contribution is payable, having regard to sections 1(6)(a), 6(2) and 6(3)` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 500) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a Class 1B contribution payable: barred by s 6(2)
#ASSERT `s 6 a primary Class 1 contribution is payable, having regard to sections 1(6)(a), 6(2) and 6(3)` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 500) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- paid after pensionable age: barred by s 6(3); but not if prescribed otherwise
#ASSERT `s 6 a primary Class 1 contribution is payable, having regard to sections 1(6)(a), 6(2) and 6(3)` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 500) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6 a primary Class 1 contribution is payable, having regard to sections 1(6)(a), 6(2) and 6(3)` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 500) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- below the primary threshold with no bar: the text's no
#ASSERT `s 6 a primary Class 1 contribution is payable, having regard to sections 1(6)(a), 6(2) and 6(3)` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 199) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not over 16: not covered (a flat negative bar is absent, the opening words do not fit)
#ASSERT `s 6 a primary Class 1 contribution is payable, having regard to sections 1(6)(a), 6(2) and 6(3)` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 500) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST FALSE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- secondary whole: the pensionable-age bar is on primary contributions only ("without prejudice to any liability to pay secondary Class 1 contributions")
#ASSERT `s 6 a secondary Class 1 contribution is payable, having regard to sections 1(6)(a) and 6(2)` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 500) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6 a secondary Class 1 contribution is payable, having regard to sections 1(6)(a) and 6(2)` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 500) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6 a secondary Class 1 contribution is payable, having regard to sections 1(6)(a) and 6(2)` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 500) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- S4 seam: weeks (100, paid), (250, not paid), (300, paid): 100 + 300 = 400
#ASSERT `s 6 the earnings on which primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid in the tax year` (LIST (`s 6 Week of earnings` OF 100, TRUE), (`s 6 Week of earnings` OF 250, FALSE), (`s 6 Week of earnings` OF 300, TRUE)) EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `s 6 the earnings on which primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid in the tax year` EMPTY EQUALS 0

§§ `s 6A`

-- s 6A(1): the amount is not less than the lower earnings limit (100) but does not exceed the primary threshold (200)
#ASSERT `s 6A(1) section 6A applies to the earnings` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 100) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6A(1) section 6A applies to the earnings` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 200) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6A(1) section 6A applies to the earnings` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 99.99) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6A(1) section 6A applies to the earnings` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 200.01) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6A(1) section 6A applies to the earnings` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 150) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST FALSE) `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6A(1) section 6A applies to the earnings` (`ssc1 fixture paid` 150) `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` NOTHING `ssc1 fixture contract of service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6A(2): each purpose
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the earner is treated as having actually paid a primary Class 1 contribution for the week` (JUST TRUE) `s 6A(3)(a) the purposes of section 14(1)(a)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the earner is treated as having actually paid a primary Class 1 contribution for the week` (JUST TRUE) `s 6A(3)(b) the purposes of the provisions mentioned in section 21(5A)(a) to (c)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the earner is treated as having actually paid a primary Class 1 contribution for the week` (JUST TRUE) `s 6A(3)(b) the purposes of the provisions mentioned in section 21(5A)(a) to (c)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the earner is treated as having actually paid a primary Class 1 contribution for the week` (JUST TRUE) `s 6A(3)(c) any other purposes relating to contributory benefits` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the earner is treated as having actually paid a primary Class 1 contribution for the week` (JUST TRUE) `s 6A(3)(d) any purposes relating to jobseeker's allowance` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the earner is treated as having actually paid a primary Class 1 contribution for the week` (JUST TRUE) `s 6A(3)(e) any purposes relating to employment and support allowance` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the earner is treated as having actually paid a primary Class 1 contribution for the week` (JUST TRUE) `s 6A(3) any other purpose` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- section 6A not applying, or a prescribed exception: not covered
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the earner is treated as having actually paid a primary Class 1 contribution for the week` NOTHING `s 6A(3)(a) the purposes of section 14(1)(a)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6A(2) the earner is treated as having actually paid a primary Class 1 contribution for the week` (JUST TRUE) `s 6A(3)(a) the purposes of section 14(1)(a)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6A(5), (6)
#ASSERT `s 6A(5) section 6A applies in relation to the earnings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6A(5) section 6A applies in relation to the earnings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6A(5) section 6A applies in relation to the earnings` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6A(6) the earnings counted for this employment` 150 700 FALSE EQUALS JUST 150
#ASSERT `s 6A(6) the earnings counted for this employment` 150 700 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 7`

-- s 7(1): contract of service: the employer; office: the prescribed person, else the paying body; regulations under (2) displace both
#ASSERT `s 7(1) who the secondary contributor is` `ssc1 fixture contract of service` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 7(1)(a) the employer`
#ASSERT `s 7(1) who the secondary contributor is` `ssc1 fixture office` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 7(1)(b)(i) the person prescribed in relation to the office`
#ASSERT `s 7(1) who the secondary contributor is` `ssc1 fixture office` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 7(1)(b)(ii) the government department, public authority or body of persons responsible for paying the earnings of the office`
#ASSERT `s 7(1) who the secondary contributor is` `ssc1 fixture contract of service` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 7(2) the person prescribed by regulations under subsection (2)`
#ASSERT `s 7(1) who the secondary contributor is` `ssc1 fixture own business` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(2B) the thing is an arrangement` `s 2(2ZB) a scheme` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(2B) the thing is an arrangement` `s 2(2ZB) something else` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 8`

-- s 8(2): the percentages the Act states (8% = 0.08, 2% = 0.02)
#ASSERT `s 8(2)(a) the main primary percentage as the Act states it` EQUALS 0.08
#ASSERT `s 8(2)(b) the additional primary percentage as the Act states it` EQUALS 0.02
-- s 8(1) with PT 200 and UEL 1000. Earnings 1500: 8% x (1000 - 200) = 64, plus 2% x (1500 - 1000) = 10; total 74.
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the amount of the primary Class 1 contribution` (JUST TRUE) 1500 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (8%) (2%) EQUALS JUST 74
-- earnings 500: 8% x (500 - 200) = 24
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the amount of the primary Class 1 contribution` (JUST TRUE) 500 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (8%) (2%) EQUALS JUST 24
-- earnings exactly at the upper earnings limit: 8% x 800 = 64 and nothing above
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the amount of the primary Class 1 contribution` (JUST TRUE) 1000 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (8%) (2%) EQUALS JUST 64
-- earnings 1000.01: 64 plus 2% x 0.01 = 0.0002
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the amount of the primary Class 1 contribution` (JUST TRUE) 1000.01 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (8%) (2%) EQUALS JUST 64.0002
-- earnings exactly at the primary threshold: nothing above it
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the amount of the primary Class 1 contribution` (JUST TRUE) 200 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (8%) (2%) EQUALS JUST 0
-- a different percentage supplied (an alteration under the Administration Act): 10% x 300 = 30
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the amount of the primary Class 1 contribution` (JUST TRUE) 500 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (10%) (2%) EQUALS JUST 30
-- not payable, or not decided: the amount is not covered
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the amount of the primary Class 1 contribution` (JUST FALSE) 500 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (8%) (2%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the amount of the primary Class 1 contribution` NOTHING 500 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (8%) (2%) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 9, s 9A, s 9B`

#ASSERT `s 9(2) the secondary percentage as the Act states it` EQUALS 0.15
-- s 9B(2): relevant apprentice = under 25 AND employed as an apprentice
#ASSERT `s 9B(2) the earner is a relevant apprentice` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9B(2) the earner is a relevant apprentice` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9B(2) the earner is a relevant apprentice` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9B(2) the earner is a relevant apprentice` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9B(2) the earner is a relevant apprentice` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 9B(1)
#ASSERT `s 9B(1) section 9B applies to the earnings` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9B(1) section 9B applies to the earnings` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9B(1) section 9B applies to the earnings` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9B(1) section 9B applies to the earnings` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 9A(1), (1A)
#ASSERT `s 9A(1) section 9A applies to the earnings` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9A(1) section 9A applies to the earnings` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9A(1) section 9A applies to the earnings` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9A(1) section 9A applies to the earnings` (JUST TRUE) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9A(1) section 9A applies to the earnings` (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 9(1A): 9B first (0%), then 9A (age-related, here 5%), otherwise the secondary percentage (15%)
#ASSERT `s 9(1A) the relevant percentage` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (5%) (15%) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 9(1A) the relevant percentage` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (5%) (15%) EQUALS JUST 0.05
#ASSERT `s 9(1A) the relevant percentage` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (5%) (15%) EQUALS JUST 0.15
#ASSERT `s 9(1A) the relevant percentage` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (5%) (15%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(1A) the relevant percentage` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (5%) (15%) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 9(1) with ST 150 and earnings 1150. Ordinary: 15% x 1000 = 150.
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution` (JUST TRUE) 1150 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (5%) (15%) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST 150
-- age group (5%), no upper secondary threshold: 5% x 1000 = 50
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution` (JUST TRUE) 1150 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (5%) (15%) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST 50
-- age group (5%) with upper secondary threshold 1000: 5% x (1000 - 150) = 42.5, plus 15% x (1150 - 1000) = 22.5; total 65
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution` (JUST TRUE) 1150 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (5%) (15%) (JUST 1000) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 65
-- relevant apprentice (0%), no upper secondary threshold: nothing at all
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution` (JUST TRUE) 1150 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (5%) (15%) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0
-- relevant apprentice with upper secondary threshold 900: 0% up to 900, then 15% x (1150 - 900) = 37.5
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution` (JUST TRUE) 1150 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (5%) (15%) (JUST 1000) (JUST 900) EQUALS JUST 37.5
-- earnings exactly at the upper secondary threshold: nothing above it
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution` (JUST TRUE) 900 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (5%) (15%) NOTHING (JUST 900) EQUALS JUST 0
-- earnings exactly at the secondary threshold (150): nothing
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution` (JUST TRUE) 150 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (5%) (15%) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0
-- not payable, or not decided: not covered
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution` (JUST FALSE) 1150 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (5%) (15%) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution` NOTHING 1150 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (5%) (15%) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution` (JUST TRUE) 1150 `ssc1 fixture limits 2030` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (5%) (15%) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 9A(5): a percentage for an added age group must be lower than the secondary percentage (15%)
#ASSERT `s 9A(5) the percentage may be specified for an added age group` (14%) (15%) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9A(5) the percentage may be specified for an added age group` (15%) (15%) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9A(5) the percentage may be specified for an added age group` (16%) (15%) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 9A(6), 9B(3): still liable though the amount is 0
#ASSERT `s 9A(6) the person is regarded as liable to pay a secondary Class 1 contribution` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9A(6) the person is regarded as liable to pay a secondary Class 1 contribution` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9B(3) the person is regarded as liable to pay a secondary Class 1 contribution` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9B(3) the person is regarded as liable to pay a secondary Class 1 contribution` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 9A(8), 9B(5): section 5(5) applies to an upper secondary threshold's equivalent
#ASSERT `s 9A(8) the regulations may prescribe the amount as an equivalent of the upper secondary threshold` 101 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9A(8) the regulations may prescribe the amount as an equivalent of the upper secondary threshold` 102 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9B(5) the regulations may prescribe the amount as an equivalent of the upper secondary threshold for relevant apprentices` 101 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9B(5) the regulations may prescribe the amount as an equivalent of the upper secondary threshold for relevant apprentices` 102 100 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 9A(10)
#ASSERT `s 9A(10) the earner falls within an age group for the purposes of subsections (7) to (9)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9A(10) the earner falls within an age group for the purposes of subsections (7) to (9)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
